# Line endings are pinned so that what is committed is what is published.
#
# The v0.1.0 and v0.1.1 releases copied files out of a Windows checkout that had
# been converted to CRLF by the host's core.autocrlf. The released install.ps1
# therefore differed byte-for-byte from the committed script, and its published
# SHA-256 could not be reproduced from the repository. `eol=lf` makes the
# checkout reproduce the committed bytes on every platform, so a workspace copy
# is the committed file. scripts/release/package-windows.ps1 still normalises and
# verifies the script it publishes, because a guard is worth more than a setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary fixtures must never be converted.
*.bin binary
*.exe binary
*.png binary
*.ico binary
*.zip binary
